 "window": "32 episodes in a session, 2 at a time: the size of a real commissioning window. A plant gives the engineer who commissions a controller for a new kit family one working shift on the cell and a tray of pre-series kits (16 here). A trial takes about a quarter of an hour: a technician lays the kit out, the cell runs at most one takt (85 s), the engineer looks at the result and the logs, the technician clears the pegs, the engineer changes the program. That is 32 trials in 8 hours, two per kit on average. Every episode is a real kit on the cell of the day (its own actual values within the data sheet's tolerances, the same every time that kit is laid out) and runs under the graded episode's limits (the takt's steps, the safety stops, the controller budget and image charges); a request may take up to silence_s, so that a hand-driven teach-in is possible.",
